ry":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Shenandoah County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. August to September came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, May to June ran 181% of normal and November to December ran 40%. Every one of the 8 grids had its driest year in 1965, and grid 22407 got just 69% of normal that year.</p>"}
